<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">T. E. Lawrence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888–1935</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lawrence of Arabia, Thomas Edward Lawrence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">T. E. Lawrence was a British archaeologist, army officer and writer. Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> he worked on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a> excavations at Carchemish from 1911 to 1914, partly alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonard-woolley">Leonard Woolley</a>. During the war he served as a liaison officer with the Arab Revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, which he described in Seven Pillars of Wisdom, and became famous as Lawrence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/t-e-lawrence.jpg" alt="T. E. Lawrence" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp;amp; Ewing · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Te_lawrence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
